id: analysis
name: Analysis
type: standard
actionCost: 1
kiCost: 0
attacking: false
requiresTarget: true
special: true
analysis: true
usageLimit: 1/round
source: Core Rule
description: >
  Read an Opponent. They are Analyzed until the end of your next turn, and your
  Combat Rolls against them gain 1(T) plus a quarter of your Scholarship Modifier.
text: >
  Analysis Maneuver [1/Round]: Study your opponents and find the perfect vital point
  to strike.
  –Maneuver Type: Standard Maneuver
  –Action Cost: 1 Action
  –Minions: Free
  –KP Cost: N/A
  –Exploitable: N/A
  –Effect: Target an Opponent. They become Analyzed until the end of your next turn.
  Increase your Combat Rolls against Analyzed Opponents by 1(T)+1/4 (rounded up) of
  your Scholarship Modifier.

---

# The first Special Maneuver, and the entry is what settled what Special means here:
# "Maneuver Type: Standard Maneuver". So Special is not a kind of Maneuver - it is
# something a Maneuver of any kind can be, and what makes one Special is that you have
# not got it until an effect gives it to you.
#
# No script. The mark goes on somebody else and the bonus is measured against them,
# and the language has no way to say either: a passive writes Slots onto the character
# holding it, and both halves of this are about a pair.
#
# What it comes to:
#   - the target is marked Analyzed, a Condition with no effects of its own
#   - the clock sits on you, not on them: "until the end of YOUR next turn" is your
#     turn, and a duration one character keeps over another is what `on` is for
#   - that clock is also the record of who Analyzed whom, which is what makes "your
#     Combat Rolls" answerable without a second place to keep it
#   - the bonus is 1(T) plus a quarter of your Scholarship Modifier rounded up, and it
#     is applied where a per-target adjustment is already applied
#
# --- The reading of "your Combat Rolls against Analyzed Opponents" ------------------
#
# Taken as: yours against the Opponent you Analyzed. The other reading is that any
# Analyzed Opponent is fair game for anybody who has this Maneuver, and the sentence
# will carry it - "Analyzed Opponents" is plural and unowned.
#
# The narrower one is built because it is the one that cannot be wrong by accident: if
# two characters Analyze two different Opponents, nobody gets a bonus they did not
# work for. If the wider reading is meant, the change is the one line that asks whose
# clock it is.
#
# --- What is not built, and why ------------------------------------------------------
#
# "Minions: Free." There are no Minions in this system - the Arrogant Declaration file
# says the same thing about its own Minion limit, and for the same reason: there is no
# notion here of whose Minions somebody is. The line is carried as printed and what it
# buys is the table's.
#
# The Wound Roll. "Combat Rolls" is the Strike, the Dodge and the Wound Roll, and the
# first two are measured against one Opponent at a time - which is where this bonus
# goes in. A Wound Roll is one roll for everyone an attack reaches, so a bonus that
# applies to some of them and not others has to be applied where the Damage is worked
# out per person, and it is: the same place a Guard halves it.
